@startuml scenario1-product-ordering-application-onboarding-sequence
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

box "Channel Partner" #LightBlue
participant "Product Order\nCapture & Validation\nPOCV TMFC002" as CPPOCV
participant "TMFC001\n---\nCommercial||Provider Catalog" as CPCat
participant "Product Order\nOrchestration\nPOOM TMFC003" as POOM
participant "Party Role\n&Permissions\nManagement\nTMFC035" as CPRole
end box

box "CSP France" #LightYellow
participant "Party Management\nTMFC028" as FRParty
participant "Resource Inventory\nTMFC008" as FRRes
participant "Party Role\n&Permissions\nManagement\nTMFC035" as FRRole
participant "POCV\nTMFC002" as FRPOCV
end box

box "CSP Belgium" #Lavender
participant "Party Management\nTMFC028" as BEParty
participant "Resource Inventory\nTMFC008" as BERes
participant "Party Role\n&Permissions\nManagement\nTMFC035" as BERole
participant "POCV\nTMFC002" as BEPOCV
end box

== Delegation to the POOM ==
CPPOCV -> POOM : 1: TMF622: POST ProductOrderStateChangeEvent\n(orderId="001", productOrder{...},state="accepted")
POOM --> CPPOCV : 2: 200 OK
note left of CPPOCV : Order placed by Tom has Id=001

== Retrieving Order Details ==
POOM -> CPPOCV : 3: TMF622: GET /productOrder/001
CPPOCV --> POOM : 4: 200 OK\n(orderDate, orderStatus,\nproductOffering.id, relatedParty, OrderItem)\n(for FR + BEL)

== Retrieving Product Offering Details ==
note over POOM : The category "Camara" and commercial attributes are retrieved\nfrom the Channel Partner Catalog.
POOM -> CPCat : 5: TMF620: GET\n/productOffering/{productOffering.id}
CPCat --> POOM : 6: ProductOffering (incl. category="Camara")

== Start Delivery Process ==
POOM -> POOM : 7: Start fulfillment workflow

== Onboarding ApplicationOwner CSP-France ==
POOM -> FRParty : 8: TMF931: POST /applicationOwnerOrganization\n(name: CountryTour, contactMedium(...))
FRParty -> FRParty : 9: internal checks\nparty not found
note right of FRParty
  The TMF931 specification does not allow for the direct creation of a Party entity.
  Currently, a Party is instantiated implicitly during the creation of
  the Party Role 'ApplicationOwner' (Refer to Note:Additionnal Context).
  We propose an enhancement to the API
  to enable the independent creation of a Party entity,
  separate from the Party Role, through the introduction
  of a dedicated endpoint: /applicationOwnerOrganization.
end note
FRParty --> POOM : 10: 201 Created\n(id: ownerFR-12345)

== Assign ApplicationOwner Role CSP-France ==
POOM -> FRRole : 11: TMF931: POST /applicationOwner\n(role: applicationOwner, partyId: ownerFR-12345, applicationId: appFR-67890)
FRRole -> FRRole : 12: internal checks
FRRole --> POOM : 13: 201 Created\n(id: roleFR-abcde, role: applicationOwner)

== Onboarding Application CSP-France ==
POOM -> FRRes : 14: TMF931: POST /application\n(name: ZoneDeals, relatedParty: ownerFR-12345, status: active)
FRRes -> FRRes : 15: internal checks\napplication not found
FRRes --> POOM : 16: 201 Created\n(id: appFR-67890)

== Onboarding ApplicationOwner CSP-Belgium ==
POOM -> BEParty : 17: TMF931: POST /applicationOwnerOrganization\n(name: CountryTour, contactMedium(...))
BEParty -> BEParty : 18: internal checks\nparty not found
note right of BEParty
  The TMF931 specification does not allow for the direct creation of
  a Party entity.
  Currently, a Party is instantiated implicitly during the creation of
  the Party Role 'ApplicationOwner' (Refer to Note:Additionnal Context).
  We propose an enhancement to the API to enable the independent
  creation of a Party entity, separate from the Party Role,
  through the introduction of a dedicated endpoint
  /applicationOwnerOrganization.
end note
BEParty --> POOM : 19: 201 Created\n(id: ownerBE-12345)

== Assign ApplicationOwner Role CSP-Belgium ==
POOM -> BERole : 20: TMF931: POST /applicationOwner\n(role: applicationOwner, partyId: ownerBE-12345, applicationId: appBE-67890)
BERole -> BERole : 21: internal checks
BERole --> POOM : 22: 201 Created\n(id: roleBE-abcde, role: applicationOwner)

== Onboarding Application CSP-Belgium ==
POOM -> BERes : 23: TMF931: POST /application\n(name: ZoneDeals, relatedParty: ownerBE-12345, status: active)
BERes -> BERes : 24: internal checks\napplication not found
BERes --> POOM : 25: 201 Created\n(id: appBE-67890)

== Product Order France ==
POOM -> FRPOCV : 26: TMF931: POST /apiProductOrder\n(externalId: order-001, relatedParty(ownerFR-12345), orderItem(...))
FRPOCV -> FRPOCV : 27: internal checks\nof order details
FRPOCV --> POOM : 28: 201 Created\n(orderId: poFR-0001, status: acknowledged)
note over FRPOCV : Starting orderdelivery on CSP side
FRPOCV -> POOM : 29: TMF931 Event: productOrderStateChangeEvent\n(orderId:poFR-0001, state:completed)
POOM --> FRPOCV : 30: 200 ok

== Product Order Belgium ==
POOM -> BEPOCV : 31: TMF931: POST /apiProductOrder\n(externalId: order-001, relatedParty(ownerBE-12345), orderItem(...))
BEPOCV -> BEPOCV : 32: internal checks\nof order details
BEPOCV --> POOM : 33: 201 Created\n(orderId: poBE-0001, status:acknowledged)
note over BEPOCV : Starting orderdelivery on CSP side
BEPOCV -> POOM : 34: TMF931 Event: productOrderStateChangeEvent\n(orderId:poBE-0001, state:completed)
POOM --> BEPOCV : 35: 200 ok

== Channel Partner Application Role Creation ==
POOM -> CPRole : 36: TMF669: POST /partyRole\n(role: applicationApiConsumer, partyId: ownerCP-12345, applicationId: appCP-67890)
CPRole --> POOM : 37: 201 Created\n(id=roleCP-abcde)

@enduml
